  "summary": "The paper compares four fabricated multilayer Ti3C2Tx electrodes: pristine, Na\u2212, K\u2212, and Mg\u2212Ti3C2Tx. All were made by LiCl-assisted 10 wt % HF etching of Ti3AlC2 followed by cation exchange, except the HCl-treated pristine control. K\u2212Ti3C2Tx is the headline and best-performing sample, reaching up to 300 F/g and \u223c5.7 F/cm2 at 20.1 mg/cm2 loading and 103 \u03bcm thickness in 1 M H2SO4. The article does not report BET area, pore size, porosity, tortuosity, or lateral flake dimensions, and several areal-capacitance maxima are only graphically presented."
